From: Ely Office
Subject: Writer: a kit client renumbers one list item

- Word's right click on an automatic number offers a new start value,
  continue numbering and the item's own number style (#147). The
  kernel's paragraph dialog path ignores a start value without the
  restart flag, and Continue Numbering moves only the selected
  paragraph, so the rest of its list keeps counting apart.
- .uno:ElyNumberFrom takes Start, 1 or more: the item at the cursor
  restarts its level there; parents and other lists keep their
  numbers. Its state is the item's number, empty off a numbered item.
- .uno:ElyNumberJoin: on a list's first item, that item and the rest
  of its list join the numbered list before it, as one undo step; an
  item with its own style keeps it. On a restarted item it clears the
  restart. Its state is disabled where neither applies.
- .uno:ElyNumberFormat takes Format, "type|pattern", type a
  css.style.NumberingType number and # the item's own number: the item
  gets a copy of its list style with that level changed, still counted
  in its list (DOCX writes it as a level override of the same list).
  Parent numbers before the level stay. A bad format changes nothing.

